{"sha":"ea62fd9679f8c6fc5e79471b33cfbd8227bfed72","node_id":"MDY6Q29tbWl0MTQwMjc2NDg6ZWE2MmZkOTY3OWY4YzZmYzVlNzk0NzFiMzNjZmJkODIyN2JmZWQ3Mg==","commit":{"author":{"name":"Stefan Berger","email":"stefanb@linux.vnet.ibm.com","date":"2021-07-23T01:23:58Z"},"committer":{"name":"Stefan Berger","email":"stefanb@us.ibm.com","date":"2021-08-04T12:58:06Z"},"message":"tpm2: Initialize a whole OBJECT before using it\n\nInitialize a whole OBJECT before using it. This is necessary since\nan OBJECT may also be used as a HASH_OBJECT via the ANY_OBJECT\nunion and that HASH_OBJECT can leave bad size inidicators in TPM2B\nbuffer in the OBJECT. To get rid of this problem we reset the whole\nOBJECT to 0 before using it. This is as if the memory for the\nOBJECT was just initialized.\n\nSigned-off-by: Stefan Berger <stefanb@linux.ibm.com>","tree":{"sha":"35d748d762ef6375aabffad2df1327f057b5025e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stefanberger/libtpms/git/trees/35d748d762ef6375aabffad2df1327f057b5025e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stefanberger/libtpms/git/commits/ea62fd9679f8c6fc5e79471b33cfbd8227bfed72","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stefanberger/libtpms/commits/ea62fd9679f8c6fc5e79471b33cfbd8227bfed72","html_url":"https://github.com/stefanberger/libtpms/commit/ea62fd9679f8c6fc5e79471b33cfbd8227bfed72","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stefanberger/libtpms/commits/ea62fd9679f8c6fc5e79471b33cfbd8227bfed72/comments","author":{"login":"stefanberger","id":1873348,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NzMzNDg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1873348?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefanberger","html_url":"https://github.com/stefanberger","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefanberger/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefanberger/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api